hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to the  edition of ask Evan I just closed my  video here today I'm answering a  question let me find it no not that one  back back back back back back back here  from Marty's all right so Marty wrote in  saying hey Evan I have a question  instead of blazing the trail on your own  where do you go about finding business  partners or even better mastermind  partners who are the same level as you  are and will help you to create better  ideas and be more productive it seems  like it's the hardest thing in the world  to find those types of people so thanks  for the question Marty's a great  question coming from a YouTube viewer it  is tough and congratulations to you at  least a start for knowing that you can't  do everything on your own and for  looking for help a lot of entrepreneurs  are afraid to ask for help try to do  within themselves and you're you're  always limited right you you cannot do  everything yourself you don't have the  skill set or the knowledge and the most  successful entrepreneurs are the ones  who reach out to get help and it may not  be a business partner or a mastermind  partner but they are going out looking  for help and recognizing that they don't  know everything themselves so Congrats  already making it past that step and  recognizing that you you know do need to  go find some people to help grow so you  ask about business partners you ask  about math my groups for the business  partners it's like getting married you  know you have to really really really  know the person before you jump into  business together and I think a lot of  entrepreneurs make the mistake of  finding somebody who has a good skill  set that matches what they're you know  not good at so if you're good at  operations or creating the product and  you partner up somebody's really good at  sales it makes sense on paper right you  have the skills that complement each  other but it doesn't mean you're going  to get along or have the same vision or  have the same personality and have the  same values right just the things you  look for when you're getting married  right do we have the same values we want  the same thing do we have personalities  that that will work well together or not  and in the first year or so of business  it's easy to get going and get excited  because you got the momentum going you  know you you have the energy and  excitement that comes with a startup and  so everybody is on the same page but  after that you start to hit roadblocks  and it gets tougher than you ever  thought it would be and you have bills  that are due and it becomes really hard  and so that's when partnerships can  break apart and come you know have have  a lot of challenges that are associated  with them and so you really want to make  sure you do your work before you go out  and and bring on you know partners into  your business  I've had some businesses with business  partners in the past and how I've always  done it is I've worked with the person  in some capacity before so it's not just  you know meeting somebody at random or  we've got an event and striking up you  know a business partnership we might try  something small some kind of joint  venture some small deal on the side see  how we work together see if it's a good  fit or not see if I get excited about  you know the phone call or meeting  that's coming up with that person and  and try to get through some kind of hard  point with them you know try to go  through some kind of struggle you know  before you get married you want to have  gone through some tough times as well  and not just experienced it good because  you want to know you can last together  through the hard times and so the same  thing with a business partnership I  would start it off with something small  part time on the side see if you guys  work together and then try to expand it  out I've always started businesses with  people who I know from some kind of  background before so it wasn't going in  cold it was people who had some kind of  relationship with and thought that we  you know could be able to work together  as business partners on the mastermind  group side that's another great  opportunity and we run a couple of  mastermind groups here in Toronto for  local entrepreneurs who are trying to  grow their business and I think of it as  an informal Board of Advisors so with a  business partner then you own part of  your company with a mastermind group  they don't own part of your but your  company but you're all just trying to  help each other out and I have a  worksheet that explains how we recruit  members and  the way we run a group that may be  helpful for you if you're trying to  start a group but really you have to  make sure again you do your homework and  a lot of these groups will just bring in  a warm body  you know anybody because they're  interested in signing up you have to  make sure you take them through a  process to make sure they're going to  fit with the group and it's not just a  skill set and it's not just the size of  their business and expertise but again  thinking about the personality and are  they of the right mindset or not to be  able to fit into the group so for our  groups we look for people who are beyond  the startup stage we look for people who  are wanting to grow business beyond  themselves and there's nothing wrong  with people who are set ups there are  nothing wrong with people who want to be  one person show it just doesn't fit with  our group you know if I tried to bring  something like that into one of our  groups they would say no because it just  doesn't fit so you have to define what  each group is about I meet with  everybody over coffee and we see you  know I learn about their business and I  get to know their personality and I see  that is this somebody who I would want  to hang out with you know a lot of the  people in our groups are kind of like me  same kind of personality and that's fun  you know it's fun for me because I want  to be around people who who I get energy  from and who I like hanging around and  not people who I don't look forward to  seeing every month right so I meet with  them over coffee we talk about the group  there's a whole process they have to go  through there's an envier they have to  sign is that there's a one-page letter  they have to write there's a trial  meeting that they have to have and so it  really helps weed out the people and  make sure that when you're bringing  somebody in to be officially part of the  group then they are accepted in terms of  how to find the people a lot of it comes  from online so we set up a website  talking about creating the groups some  of our process and people are searching  for all sorts of different keywords and  they end up finding us and contacting me  a little bit happens to the word of  mouth I think some of our members have  come from people who are existing  members and they referred their their  friends and colleagues on a lot of  people who join the groups it's tough  because as entrepreneur you don't have a  lot of other entrepreneurs who you can  connect with on a regular basis not  Sophie  back on you know we may have friends and  family and they they like to listen but  they maybe can't provide support because  they don't know they haven't been  through what you're going through and so  if you had a really good support network  of entrepreneurs you probably wouldn't  be looking to join a mastermind group so  a lot of the members don't necessarily  know other people who would be good fits  and so it's it's you know your role if  you're organizing it to you know be the  one out recruiting create a webpage  promote a little bit and get people  interested you may be the phone some  partnerships with other entrepreneur  groups or government organizations who  are promoting to entrepreneurs and  here's another resource for them to  follow up on almost every city has some  kind of government organization that is  trying to help entrepreneurs out so you  know let them know that you're trying to  create these groups maybe they'll even  help you out with it but you have to  make sure you do your homework and you  think about getting the right people in  and skill sets you need and the  personality fits and and you know do you  want to spend the next year with these  people are not are they going to help  your business or not so it is definitely  definitely a tough road but one worth  following and think about it again for  me the partnership side or for started a  mastermind group to do your work you  know make sure you know what you're  looking for in advance try something out  small to start with and then invite you  know then invite them for a potential  further opportunity if it's a business  partnership or mastermind group but but  keep looking out keep reaching out don't  get frustrated by the process and think  you're gonna have to do everything  yourself because that's always going to  limit your thinking and how big your  business is going to be able to grow so  thank you for the question hopefully  that helped for those of you watching if  you like the video please give it a  thumbs up below it always makes you want  to do more videos for you and if you  have a comment about the partnerships or  mastermind groups or another question  about your business feel free to leave  it in the comment section below I always  read those and I always answer those  good as I can they always make my day  when they do come in so thank you and  I'll see you on the next episode
 

